Instruments: $\mathrm{^{1}H}$ nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR） data to confirm the ligand synthesis and incorporation of R-isoph and TPTC in each R(N)-PCN-125 were recorded on a Mercury 300 spectrometer at the Center for Chemical Characterization and Analysis (CCCA), Department of Chemistry, Texas A&M University.FT-IR data was collected by use of an IRAffinity-1 instrument. To obtain the TGA data, a TGA-5O (SHIMADZU) thermogravimetric analyzer was used with a heating rate of $s^{\circ}C$ $\mathrm{min^{-1}}$ under $\mathbf{N}_{2}$ flow. The powder X-ray diffraction patterns (PXRD) were recorded by a BRUKER D8-Focus Bragg-Brentano X-ray Powder diffractometer equipped with a Cu sealed tube $\langle{\lambda=}$ 1.54178 A) at a scan rate of $0.5\ \mathrm{s\deg^{-1}}$ . All gas adsorption meas urements were performed by Micromeritics' ASAP 2020 with the extra-pure quality gases.   Based on the adsorption branch of $\Nu_{2}$ adsorption isotherms of R(N)-PCN-l25, the pore size distributions were calculated by using density functional theory (DFT） or Kruk-Jaroniec-Sayari (KJS） method in the Barrett-JoynerHalenda (BJH) algorithm2², provided by ASAP 2020 software.
