Synthesis of R(N)-PCN-125: a mixture of $\mathrm{{H_{4}T P T C}}$ $(40\mathrm{mg},0.1$ mmol), R-isoph (0.1 or $0.2\ \mathrm{mmol}$ , amounts indicated in Table S1) and $\mathrm{Cu}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}3\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ $(120~\mathrm{\mg},~0.5~\mathrm{\mmol})$ in $15~\mathrm{\mL}$ N,Ndimethylacetamide (DMA) was sealed in a glass vial. The vial was tightly capped and placed in an $85^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ oven for $48\mathrm{h}$ to yield blue or green crystaline powders. For further analysis such as gas adsorption, PXRD and NMR measurement, the crystalline powder samples were washed with fresh DMA $\mathrm{\Omega}20\mathrm{mL},$ ) and then immersed in fresh DMA $(20~\mathrm{mL})$ ）for l day. Thorough washing with DMA is necessary to remove unreacted ligands in the crystals and the NMR peaks of the ligands after digesting R(N)-PCN-125 becomes solely from the crystal and not from the surface adsorbed one. Phase purity of all products was evaluated by powder X-ray diffraction (PXRD). General characterizations including IR and TGA were carried out and given in SI.
Gas adsorption. Gas adsorption measurements were performed using an ASAP 2020 volumetric adsorption analyzer. A high purity grade of gases was used throughout the adsorption experiments. Before adsorption, the sample was immersed in dry methanol for $^{72\mathrm{~h~}}$ to remove the nonvolatile solvates. After draining the methanol, chloroform was subsequently added, and the sample was allowed to sit for $^{72\mathrm{{h}}}$ . After the removal of chloroform, the sample was dried under a dynamic vacuum $\mathrm{(<0.1\mmHg)}$ ）at room temperature overnight and then activated again at $100^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ by using the degassing port in ASAP 2020.
